      "writtenOn": "2024-09-10T16:26:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`aseert()`, should call `abort()`, which will [call `raise(SIGABRT)`](https://sourceware.org/git/?p\u003dnewlib-cygwin.git;a\u003dblob;f\u003dnewlib/libc/stdlib/abort.c;h\u003d065dee5b6c710102420d91139434e5fd0897838a;hb\u003dHEAD#l58). `raise()` should call the newlib \"syscall\" [`_kill()`](https://sourceware.org/git/?p\u003dnewlib-cygwin.git;a\u003dblob;f\u003dlibgloss/libnosys/kill.c;h\u003d27c4f8cf667f278b05761382e368b61ef44a9a63;hb\u003dHEAD), which we can add to our `libc/syscalls.c` file. The `int sig` argument to `_kill()` should be `SIGABRT` in the `assert/abort` case. If we receive a `SIGABRT` before `_exit()` is called, then we know it was an `assert/abort`. If we don\u0027t receive that signal before `_exit()` is called, then it is just a regular exit.",
